{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: exact O4 configuration head d4b674cf199c803f34166a2894d4a16a23a09f85 on builder/o4-connect-config-20261103, for request ccd3389d under promise fdabe979 and review request be938e10. This approval covers apps/room/wrangler.connect.jsonc, the runbook docs/o4-connect.md, the settings inventory and the record. It claims no deployment, bucket, register, room, host connection or O4 acceptance.\n\nScope. Main fdeeba88 is an ancestor, and the head merges cleanly with current main 79f7d1b8. It changes the new configuration, the new runbook, docs/security/settings.md, the note and four manifests. The worktree is clean and the branch is pushed. The commit-message check passes for all 6 commits. No card path changes. From the frozen source 08127856 to the head, only the note and two manifests change.\n\nWhat holds in the configuration:\n\n- dap-connect deploys closed. MCP_ENABLED is the string \"false\", and REGISTER_SCOPE is the one placeholder.\n- OAUTH_DYNAMIC_REGISTRATION, OAUTH_CLIENT_METADATA_ORIGINS and OAUTH_REDIRECT_URIS are absent, so registration stays off and only the default Claude and ChatGPT metadata origins apply.\n- The four Durable Object bindings name this Worker's own classes under a fresh v1 migration. The R2 bucket dap-connect-application-content belongs to it alone. No binding names another Worker.\n- MCP_RESOURCE_URLS names both connector URLs. The Claude card domain 5334a0aa….claudemcpcontent.com equals the first 32 hex digits of SHA-256 of https://dap-connect.inguz.workers.dev/mcp. I recomputed it.\n- APPLICATION_TRUST holds exactly the one Grow row that dap-grow trusts: the same release, publisher and host, as ruling aa2284b3 requires.\n- The request-signal flag matches the other Workers. The creation pins name the own-agent cohort.\n\nThe guard. The Grow release's agent defaults, grow.climate and grow.sense, are not in the member default, grow.tend. The production guard predicate refuses enrollment with them (agent-role-wider) and holds without them. The runbook installs only the admin and member defaults, and step 6 rereads the roster and stops on any agent action outside the member actions. No Grow card act is open to the ordinary member's agent: take-task needs grow.tend, and the vent acts need grow.climate. So the runbook takes the ruling's fallback: a read-only card press, then a separate issue.open through the same agent. It says which one it uses and why.\n\nThe runbook. It keeps the register, home and first room together. It retains uncertain operations instead of replanning, and it keeps the secret off argument lists and out of evidence. It refuses rather than enables registration for a host without allowlisted metadata, and it closes the endpoint before the window ends. The evidence list covers host builds, both handshakes, any Origin header, screenshots, both hosts connected at once, each revocation and the optional deployed-browser probe.\n\nThe gates passed. gate.exit reads exit 0 at 08127856, tree 61127fe7, and exit 0 at the earlier checkpoint 767c825c. Both record the same clean head, tree and lockfile before and after. The pinned Wrangler 4.147.0 dry run bundles the configuration with exit 0.\n\nEvidence. The four manifests list 59 public files and index 73 private files. All match their sizes and digests, the public files are read-only, every SHA256SUMS file matches, and no unit holds an unlisted file. The credential scan matched only the private dry-run bundle, worker.js and its map. Both are compiled source that names the header pattern, and neither holds a credential. The note names all four manifests' SHA-256 values.\n\nRequired before landing, with no new head: every private original sits under /private/tmp, in artroom-o4-connect-private-20261103, artroom-o4-grow-final-private-20261103 and artroom-o4-grow-gate-private-20261103. macOS clears /private/tmp at restart, and this machine restarted this morning. Earlier heads kept their private raw files under /Users/hughpyle/play/artroom-private-evidence for at least 30 days after landing. Builder: copy all three directories there, check every hash against the private indexes, and name the new location in the landing act.\n\nArchitecture: sound. O4 gets an isolated Worker that deploys closed, and the runbook leaves every authority change to the planner's window.\n\nSecurity: no blocking finding. Nothing widens a role or guard, registration stays off, and the card press signs nothing. One check for the live window: the ChatGPT card domain is the Worker's own origin, https://dap-connect.inguz.workers.dev, which is also where the member's consent key lives. ChatGPT should render the card in its own sandbox origin. Record the card frame's actual origin. If it ever equals the Worker's origin, stop the ChatGPT scene before consent.\n\nSimplification: no required change.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:b1c327b19079ee595e8109256f72fac3cc0a23e4","binding":"assigned","head":"d4b674cf199c803f34166a2894d4a16a23a09f85","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:92b5a54ee954ad4243cadc98ab863c2ed7ce0158\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:fdabe979c58723f637ea2977efc204f28536fec1\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:db30be37023904f01ee631bf35551195c96b7a78","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}